    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (25 tests, 0 failures/errors), including the new `Cp15Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field on the owner response so it returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nTwo changes, following the existing patterns for derived owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` property (enum `SILVER`/`BRONZE`) to the `Owner` schema, so the code-generated `OwnerDto` includes the field with a `MembershipTierEnum`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes the tier from the persisted owner: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount != null && == 0` and `email` is non-null/non-blank, else `BRONZE`.\n\nThe tier is computed at mapping time from already-persisted fields (`namesakeCount` is assigned on create, `email` is stored), so it's correct on both the create response and subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}` reads.",
